{
  "requirement": "`trust_but_verify::domain::NodeContents::format` presents the retained\n{term}`requirements.sdk.graph.node_contents` as text for an agent:\n\n```rust,ignore\npub trait NodeContents: Send + Sync {\n    // ...\n\n    /// Present these retained contents as text for an agent.\n    /// Use the same observation described by fingerprint().\n    /// Everything needed for presentation is retained in this value.\n    fn format(&self) -> String;\n\n    // ...\n}\n```\n\nFormatting uses the retained value and completes without further resource reads\nor fallible preparation.",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "**Obligations derived from `requirements.sdk.graph.node_content.format`**\n1. `format()` presents the retained node contents as agent text.\n2. It uses the same observation as `fingerprint()`.\n3. Everything needed is retained in the value. Formatting does no further resource reads and no fallible preparation.\n\n**Test mapping**\n- `crates/trust-but-verify/tests/contracts.rs#fn[identities_remain_stable_and_fingerprinting_uses_the_supplied_snapshot]` is marked `{test}` for this requirement. It reads a snapshot while node 1 holds \"before\" and asserts `snapshot.content.format() == \"before\"`. It then changes the underlying resource to \"after\" and asserts three things:\n  - `snapshot.content.fingerprint()` still equals `snapshot.fingerprint`, with value \"before\".\n  - `format()` still returns \"before\".\n  - The read log is still `[1]`.\n  This covers format and fingerprint describing the same observation. It also covers format using only the retained value and doing no further resource reads.\n- `src/sdk.rs#mod[tests]/fn[domain_formats_supplied_contents_without_resolving_a_replacement]` is marked `{test}` for this requirement. It builds the production `HabeasNodeContent` from a `ResolvedInput` that names a non-existent `missing.rs` file. It asserts that `format()` contains both the supplied text and the path. Formatting therefore needs no file access and does not fail even though the file is absent.\n\n**Exemption**\n- The production `format` in `src/sdk.rs` (`impl[HabeasNodeContent/NodeContents]/fn[format]`) only clones the stored `text`, with no conditional and no transformation. `HabeasNodeContent::prepare` derives the fingerprint and the text from the same `ResolvedInput`.\n- The fallible serialization happens in `prepare`, not in `format`.\n\nI found no unmarked relevant tests and no acknowledgments. The tests cover each obligation.",
  "references": "cad441b38e5d73720a818ad7d68ca3c5ff996e1fd71c1d4c271b09a52e2b1213",
